    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293-a7">

                <pb facs="0488" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg416"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Indorsement.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Headquarters Military Division of the Missouri</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Chicago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1882-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 10, 1882.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Respectfully forwarded to the Adjutant-General of the Army.</p>
                <p>Co-operation of the troops of both countries along the frontier would
                    unquestionably be very beneficial, but it can only be effected through the
                    effort of the State Department.</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. SHERIDAN,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant-General,
                            Commanding.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
